steps=[
 step('Retain actual definitions and derive joint Borel observables','Keep the literal harmonic flow, zero-normal identity reflection, intensity, integrated hazard, first ≥ crossing, stopped recursion, Exp1 product and full finite history. Consume the verified hazard/clock, flow and rate producers; the exponential-product theorem supplies P probability internally. Distribute the record sum across raw clock/time. On live records compose joint crossing and density maps, while stopped records use zero. Coerce untopD0 for the total Borel real observer. Multiplication, exp and ofReal give jointly Borel finite density. Density at nonpositive real times and defaults at stopped/infinite waits are auxiliary total extensions, used only through the strict positive finite guards below.',r'W,\ t,\ \rho\ \text{jointly Borel},\qquad\rho<\infty.','  classical\n','  refine ⟨hw, hρ, hρfin'),
 step('Construct actual histories, strict guards and the genuine kernel','Fix any Borel finite-valued d, possibly unbounded across histories. Define H, unchanged raw tail Y, μ, guarded D, canonical density kernel K, product event Q, actual event B and pair X. The verified history theorem gives Borel H,Y and (H,Y)_*P=μ⊗P. The last-history and tail0 projections yield Borel W,G,Q and actual B,X. The guard 0<s<d(h) is jointly Borel, hence uncurry D is Borel. Mathlib withDensity_apply then proves K(h)=volume.withDensity(D(h,·)) for every abstract history: this identifies the intended measurable branch, ruling out its zero fallback.',formulae[2],'  refine ⟨hw, hρ, hρfin','  -- Restrict the deterministic'),
 step('Restrict each deterministic fiber to strict positive finite waits','A stopped last record gives an empty positive-wait event and zero density. For a live state z, producer86 gives f_*(P|A)=ρ_T with T=d(h), A={0<U≤T}, and ρ_T the density on Ioc(0,T). Restrict BOTH measures by Iio(T). Its pullback intersects A exactly in 0<U<T: top cannot satisfy the finite bound; finite waits compare via explicit NNReal/WithTop/real coercions. Restrict-map and restrict-withDensity give density on Ioc(0,T)∩Iio(T)=Ioo(0,T), namely D(h,s)ds. This restricts an equality; it never equates open/closed endpoint masses or assumes no finite atoms.',r'f_*(P|_{\{0<U\le T\}})|_{(-\infty,T)}=f_*(P|_{\{0<U<T\}})=\mathbf1_{(0,T)}(s)\rho_z(s)\,ds.','  -- Restrict the deterministic','  have hmass'),
 step('Derive a uniform kernel mass bound internally','For every fixed abstract history, the density measure is the pushforward of P restricted to the strict finite event. Its mass on all real times is that event probability, at most1. The proved fiber equality transfers this bound to K(h,ℝ), including stopped records, d(h)=0 and unrealizable histories. C=1 supplies IsFiniteKernel. This bounds mass, not the pointwise density; no finite-wait guarantee, integrability provider or normalization is used.',r'K_d(h,\mathbb R)=P\{v:0<W(h_n,v_0)<d(h)\}\le1.','  have hmass','  -- The actual complete history'),
 step('Identify the actual joint finite measure','For arbitrary Borel C⊆Hist×ℝ, pull the actual restricted pushforward back through G(H,Y). L=G⁻¹(C)∩Q is Borel. Replace the joint history/tail law by μ⊗P and apply product-measure sections. The strict fixed-history fiber law replaces each section by D(h,s)ds. Nonnegative product integration gives ∫_C D d(μ⊗ds)=ν(C). Equality for all Borel C proves the joint map law. Total mass is at most1 because ν is a restricted pushforward of the actual probability P.',formulae[3],'  -- The actual complete history','  refine ⟨hD, hK, hfinite'),
 step('Integrate every nonnegative joint test on every history event','Jointly Borel F gives jointly Borel F·D; nonnegative parameter integration makes its time integral Borel in h, allowing infinity. For arbitrary Borel A multiply F by the indicator of the first-coordinate event. Restrict/map nonnegative integration and the proved joint measure identity give its ν integral. The density formula and Tonelli yield ∫μ∫ds 1_A(h)F(h,s)D(h,s). The indicator formula gives the displayed history-restricted identity, including null A. No boundedness, integrability, positive conditioning probability, conditional representative or normalization enters.',formulae[4],'  refine ⟨hD, hK, hfinite','\nend\n')]
assert ''.join(x['lean'] for x in steps)==s[body:s.index('\nend\n',body)]
